<article class="env-corollary" id="03CW">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03CW">Corollary <span data-tag="03CW">7.5.7.9</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a commutative diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation" id="03CX">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="03CX" href="/tag/03CX">7.67</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:homotopy-pushout-as-homotopy-colimit} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  A_{0} \ar [d] \\ A_{1} \ar [r] &amp;  A_{01}, } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> which we identify with a functor $\mathscr {F}: [1] \times [1] \rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$. Then (<a data-tag="03CX" href="/tag/03CX">7.67</a>) is a homotopy pushout square (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="0113" href="/tag/0113">3.4.2.1</a>) if and only if $\mathscr {F}$ is a homotopy colimit diagram (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03CQ" href="/tag/03CQ">7.5.7.3</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Propositions <a data-tag="03CT" href="/tag/03CT">7.5.7.6</a> and <a data-tag="03BJ" href="/tag/03BJ">7.5.4.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
